.TH SAYNOW 1 "2026-07-27" "saynow 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
saynow \- speak text aloud from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saynow
[\fIoptions\fR] \fItext\fR...
.br
.B saynow
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B saynow
\fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saynow
plays synthesised speech through the speakers. It is built to be called by LLM
agents that need to tell a human something out loud, and runs with no setup by
falling back to the operating system's built-in voice.
.PP
With no text arguments and standard input not a terminal,
.B saynow
reads the text to speak from standard input.
.PP
The full reference is also available with
.BR "saynow --help" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Interactively pick a provider and store an API key.
.TP
.B config list
Print every setting and its value, with secrets redacted.
.TP
.BI "config get " key
Print one setting.
.TP
.BI "config set " "key value"
Change one setting and save it.
.TP
.B config path
Print the absolute path of the config file.
.TP
.B voices
List voice names valid for the active provider.
.TP
.B models
List OpenRouter models that can emit speech.
.TP
.B history
List archived clips, newest first. \fBhistory open\fR [\fIn\fR] plays one,
\fBhistory path\fR prints the directory, \fBhistory clear\fR deletes them all.
.TP
.B help
Show the full help text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-voice " " \fIname\fR
Voice name. Valid values differ per provider; run
.BR "saynow voices" .
Defaults to the provider's own default.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-provider " " \fIid\fR
Where speech is synthesised: \fBsystem\fR, \fBopenai\fR, \fBelevenlabs\fR or
\fBopenrouter\fR. Defaults to \fBsystem\fR, or the configured provider.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " " \fIid\fR
Model id, for providers that have models. Run
.BR "saynow models" .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rate " " \fIn\fR
Speaking rate in words per minute. The \fBsystem\fR provider only. Typical
range 150 to 350.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-speed " " \fIn\fR
Playback speed multiplier, 0.25 to 4.0. Cloud providers only; \fBopenrouter\fR
ignores it. Defaults to 1.
.TP
.B \-\-ask
Add a reply box to the bubble and wait for an answer, which is printed to
standard output. See
.B THE BUBBLE
below. Cannot be combined with \fB\-\-save\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ui
Speak without showing the bubble at all.
.TP
.BI \-\-save " file"
Write audio to \fIfile\fR instead of playing it, and print the absolute path.
Not supported by the \fBsystem\fR provider. The format is mp3, or wav for
\fBopenrouter\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-queue
Do not wait for other
.B saynow
processes. Speech from concurrent calls may overlap.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Exit non\-zero when the chosen provider is unusable, instead of falling back to
the system voice.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress warnings on standard error. Exit codes are unaffected.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the full help text.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH PROVIDERS
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
\fBsystem\fR|no credential|offline, built into the OS
\fBopenai\fR|OPENAI_API_KEY|dedicated speech endpoint
\fBelevenlabs\fR|ELEVENLABS_API_KEY|most natural, highest cost
\fBopenrouter\fR|OPENROUTER_API_KEY|15+ dedicated speech models
.TE
.PP
If a cloud provider is selected but no credential is found,
.B saynow
warns on standard error, speaks with the system voice, and exits 0. An agent
reporting success to someone who heard nothing is worse than a robotic voice.
Use
.B \-\-strict
to make this an error instead.
.PP
Concurrent
.B saynow
processes serialise through a lock file, so three calls produce three sentences
rather than one muddle.
.SH THE BUBBLE
Whenever
.B saynow
speaks it also shows a small bubble in the bottom\-right corner carrying the
transcript, lit word by word, with a stop button and a dismiss button. It fades
out shortly after the audio ends, so a sentence you half\-heard is still
readable. Pass \fB\-\-no\-ui\fR to suppress it.
.PP
On macOS the bubble is a floating panel: no Dock icon, no entry in the
application switcher, and it does not take focus from the app you are using.
Elsewhere it falls back to a Chromium application window, which looks the same
but carries a title bar. With neither available,
.B saynow
simply speaks.
.PP
\fB\-\-ask\fR adds a reply box and waits. The reply is written to standard
output, so a caller can read it directly:
.PP
.RS
.EX
answer=$(saynow --ask "Should I drop the old table?")
.EE
.RE
.PP
It waits indefinitely once you interact with it. If you do not, it fades out
five seconds after the audio ends and exits 2, which lets a caller tell
"they said no" apart from "nobody was there".
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings live in \fI~/.config/saynow/config.json\fR, created with mode 0600.
Precedence, from lowest to highest, is built\-in defaults, the config file,
environment variables, then command\-line flags.
.PP
Settings accepted by \fBconfig set\fR: \fBprovider\fR, \fBvoice\fR,
\fBmodel\fR, \fBspeed\fR, \fBhistoryLimit\fR, \fBopenaiApiKey\fR,
\fBelevenlabsApiKey\fR and \fBopenrouterApiKey\fR.
.PP
API keys are deliberately not accepted as flags, because argv is visible to
.BR ps (1)
and is saved in shell history. Use
.BR "saynow init" ,
.BR "saynow config set" ,
or the environment variable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR SAYNOW_PROVIDER ", " SAYNOW_VOICE ", " SAYNOW_MODEL ", " SAYNOW_SPEED
Equivalent to the matching command\-line flags.
.TP
.B SAYNOW_CONFIG_DIR
Override the directory holding \fIconfig.json\fR.
.TP
.B SAYNOW_LOCK_PATH
Override the playback lock file, giving this process its own queue instead of
the machine\-wide one.
.TP
.B SAYNOW_HISTORY_DIR
Override where archived clips are written.
.TP
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ", " ELEVENLABS_API_KEY ", " OPENROUTER_API_KEY
Provider credentials. These take precedence over the config file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Spoke successfully, or wrote the file when \fB\-\-save\fR was given.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, unusable provider under \fB\-\-strict\fR, network or API failure,
or no audio player found on the system.
.TP
.B 2
\fB\-\-ask\fR was dismissed or timed out without a reply.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/saynow/config.json
Configuration, mode 0600.
.TP
.I $TMPDIR/saynow.lock
Lock file serialising concurrent playback.
.SH HISTORY
Every cloud synthesis is archived, so converting a long article once means you
can replay or share it without paying for it again. The newest 50 clips are
kept; change that with \fBsaynow config set historyLimit\fR \fIn\fR, or set it
to 0 to archive nothing. The listing shows what each clip cost, looked up when
you run it rather than during synthesis, so speaking is never delayed to
learn the price. Only OpenRouter reports one. The system voice is not
archived, because it speaks directly and never produces a file.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Voice names are vendor\-specific and OpenRouter rejects a request without one.
.B saynow
ships verified voice lists for 8 of the 15 speech models; for the rest, pass
\fB\-\-voice\fR explicitly.
.PP
The
.B system
provider cannot write files, so it rejects \fB\-\-save\fR.
.PP
Windows support is best\-effort and less tested than macOS and Linux.
.SH EXAMPLES
Speak a sentence with the offline system voice:
.PP
.RS
.EX
saynow "the build finished"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Speak the last line of a command's output:
.PP
.RS
.EX
npm test 2>&1 | tail -1 | saynow
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use a specific provider, model and voice:
.PP
.RS
.EX
saynow -p openrouter -m openai/gpt-audio -v nova "routed via OpenRouter"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Write audio to a file instead of playing it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
saynow --save note.mp3 "write to a file instead of playing"
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR say (1)
on macOS,
.BR espeak-ng (1)
on Linux.
.PP
Project home: https://github.com/dhruvyad/saynow
